ror of unusual size, or a major surprise in turnout, is essentially the only path to a closer race.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts governor is among the least competitive races on the 2026 map. Incumbent Maura Healey faces Republican Mike Minogue and an independent, Andrea James. The state's 14-point Democratic lean, Healey's incumbency advantage, and a polling average near 21 points all point the same direction. Recent surveys from UNH, Suffolk, and UMass Amherst show her ahead by 19 to 25 points, and the trend has been stable all year.\n\nEvery major race rater labels the contest Solid or Safe D, and prediction markets give Healey roughly a 98% chance of winning. Minogue has disputed the public polls, but no evidence suggests a meaningful shift. The realistic question is the size of the victory margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5},